#: ../../index.rst:8
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr "Kom godt i gang"

#: ../../index.rst:11
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduktion"

#: ../../index.rst:13
msgid ""
"Welcome to the CentreStack Server Deployment Guide. This guide describes "
"deployment tasks for CentreStack, a managed file synchronization and "
"sharing solution that focuses on local file server cloud-enablement."
msgstr "Velkommen til CentreStack Server Deployment Guide. Denne guide beskriver opgaver for udrulning af CentreStack, en administreret filsynkroniserings- og delingsløsning, der fokuserer på cloud-aktivering af lokale filservere."

#: ../../index.rst:17
msgid ""
"CentreStack includes the CentreStack server, which runs on the Microsoft "
"Windows server platform, and client agent applications for Microsoft "
"Windows, Mac OS X, web browsers, Android and Apple iOS operating systems."
msgstr "CentreStack inkluderer CentreStack-serveren, som kører på Microsoft Windows-serverplatformen, og klientagentapplikationer til Microsoft Windows, Mac OS X, webbrowsere, Android og Apple iOS-operativsystemer."

#: ../../index.rst:23
msgid "This guide is updated to match build |release|"
msgstr "Denne vejledning er opdateret til at matche build |release|"

#: ../../index.rst:28
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Oversigt"

#: ../../index.rst:30
msgid ""
"CentreStack is a managed file sync and share solution that focuses on "
"local file server cloud-enablement. It differentiates from other file "
"sync and share solutions (EFSS) by focusing on security, control, file "
"server and team collaboration. CentreStack does really well in the "
"following areas:"
msgstr "CentreStack er en administreret filsynkroniserings- og delingsløsning, der fokuserer på at gøre lokale filservere cloud-aktiverede. Den adskiller sig fra andre filsynkroniserings- og delingsløsninger (EFSS) ved at fokusere på sikkerhed, kontrol, filservere og teamsamarbejde. CentreStack klarer sig virkelig godt på følgende områder:"

#: ../../index.rst:32
msgid ""
"provide on-demand access that honors read-only and write permissions in "
"real-time."
msgstr "giv adgang efter behov, der overholder læse- og skrivetilladelser i realtid."

#: ../../index.rst:33
msgid ""
"mirror local network share on file server to team collaboration in the "
"cloud."
msgstr "spejl lokalt netværksdrev på filserver til teamsamarbejde i skyen."

#: ../../index.rst:34
msgid "provide virtual drive letter mapping to the files and folders for access."
msgstr "tilvejebringe virtuel drevbogstavstilknytning til filer og mapper for adgang."

#: ../../index.rst:35
msgid ""
"provide file locking, version control, client encryption and etc features"
" for the virtual drive."
msgstr "tilbyder fil låsning, versionskontrol, klient kryptering og etc funktioner for det virtuelle drev."

#: ../../index.rst:39
msgid ""
"In summary, you can think of CentreStack as a way to elevate and turn a "
"Windows File Server in a local area network into a Cloud/Internet facing "
"file server solution with remote and mobile access, while at the same "
"time, the drive mapping, the NTFS permission, and file locking are "
"preserved before and after the cloud-enablement."
msgstr "Sammenfattende kan du tænke på CentreStack som en måde at opgradere og omdanne en Windows-filserver i et lokalt netværk til en sky-/internetbaseret filserverløsning med fjernadgang og mobiladgang, samtidig med at drevtilknytningen, NTFS-tilladelserne og filspærringen bevares før og efter skyaktiveringen."

#: ../../index.rst:43
msgid ""
"The CentreStack server is a pure software built on top of the Microsoft "
"Web Platform, which includes:"
msgstr "CentreStack-serveren er ren software bygget oven på Microsofts webplatform, som inkluderer:"

#: ../../index.rst:45
msgid "Windows Server,"
msgstr "Windows Server,"

#: ../../index.rst:46
msgid "IIS (Internet Information Server),"
msgstr "IIS (Internet Information Server)"

#: ../../index.rst:47
msgid ".NET Framework and ASP.NET"
msgstr ".NET Framework og ASP.NET"

#: ../../index.rst:48
msgid "WCF (Windows Communication Foundation)"
msgstr "WCF (Windows Communication Foundation)"

#: ../../index.rst:50
msgid ""
"Since the CentreStack server is built on top of the Microsoft Web "
"Platform, it integrates very well with Microsoft components such as NTFS "
"Permission, Active Directory, File Server network shares, file locking "
"and drive mapping."
msgstr "Da CentreStack-serveren er bygget på toppen af Microsoft Web Platform, integrerer den meget godt med Microsoft-komponenter såsom NTFS-tilladelser, Active Directory, netværksandele på filservere, filspærring og drevtilknytning."

#: ../../index.rst:54
msgid ""
"It provides file access and sharing functionality through client agents "
"for remote PCs, Macs, File Servers, Web Browsers, and Mobile Devices."
msgstr "Det giver adgang til og deling af filer via klientagenter til fjern-PC'er, Macs, filservere, webbrowsere og mobile enheder."

#: ../../index.rst:56
msgid ""
"The services can be deployed in flexible combinations to meet different "
"needs. There are two primary ways to deploy the CentreStack."
msgstr "Tjenesterne kan implementeres i fleksible kombinationer for at opfylde forskellige behov. Der er to primære måder at implementere CentreStack på."

#: ../../index.rst:58
msgid ""
"Deploy in the same site as the File Servers and Active Directory domain "
"controllers:"
msgstr "Udrul i samme site som filserverne og Active Directory-domænecontrollere:"

#: ../../index.rst:62
msgid ""
"Deploy in a remote site, such as Amazon Web Services EC2, Microsoft "
"Azure, or in a Data Center where the Managed Service Provider (MSP) hosts"
" their infrastructure:"
msgstr "Implementer på et fjernsted, såsom Amazon Web Services EC2, Microsoft Azure eller i et datacenter, hvor Managed Service Provider (MSP) hoster deres infrastruktur:"

#: ../../index.rst:70
msgid ""
"With the Hosted-CentreStack solution, the CentreStack server is already "
"deployed on https://sync4share.com. Therefore, there is no need to deploy"
" a CentreStack server. Instead, you can start using the hosted-"
"centrestack web portal and client agents directly."
msgstr "Med Hosted-CentreStack-løsningen er CentreStack-serveren allerede udrullet på https://sync4share.com. Derfor er der ikke behov for at udrulle en CentreStack-server. I stedet kan du begynde at bruge det hosted-centrestack webportal og klientagenter direkte."

#: ../../index.rst:76
msgid ""
"Moving forward, this document will refer to the deployment of the Self-"
"Hosted CentreStack server, and its related client agent applications."
msgstr "Fremadrettet vil dette dokument referere til udrulningen af den selvhostede CentreStack-server og de tilhørende klientagentapplikationer."

#: ../../index.rst:80
msgid ""
"There are three different infrastructure components (logical components "
"that can co-exist in the same server). In the smallest deployment unit, "
"the different components can co-exist in one single machine (all-in-one "
"deployment)."
msgstr "Der er tre forskellige infrastrukturkomponenter (logiske komponenter, der kan sameksistere på samme server). I den mindste udrulningsenhed kan de forskellige komponenter sameksistere i én enkelt maskine (all-in-one udrulning)."

#: ../../index.rst:85
msgid "1. Worker Node Component"
msgstr "Worker Node-komponent"

#: ../../index.rst:87
msgid ""
"Worker node contains services like Web Browser Based File Manager, "
"Storage Service Connectors, Active Directory connector and other key "
"components. It is responsible for data related activities such as file "
"upload and download, permission, control and change notification. Since "
"the data upload and download usually go through worker node, thus it is "
"called a \"worker\" for data transfer."
msgstr "Worker-noden indeholder tjenester som webbaseret filhåndtering, storage service-forbindelser, Active Directory-konnektor og andre nøglekomponenter. Den er ansvarlig for datarelaterede aktiviteter såsom filupload og -download, tilladelseskontrol og ændringsnotifikationer. Da dataupload og -download normalt går gennem worker-noden, kaldes den derfor en \"worker\" for datatransfer."

#: ../../index.rst:93
msgid "Additional nodes can be added as the load increases."
msgstr "Yderligere noder kan tilføjes, efterhånden som belastningen stiger."

#: ../../index.rst:97
msgid "2. Database Component"
msgstr "2. Databasekomponent"

#: ../../index.rst:99
msgid ""
"The database contains persistent information for the system. A Database "
"is a critical component for the smooth operation of the CentreStack "
"server farm. A Local database with latency less than 10 milliseconds is "
"recommended."
msgstr "Databasen indeholder vedvarende information for systemet. En database er en kritisk komponent for den problemfri drift af CentreStack serverfarmen. En lokal database med en latenstid på mindre end 10 millisekunder anbefales."

#: ../../index.rst:103
msgid ""
"In order for all worker nodes to be in the same server farm, they need to"
" point to the same database."
msgstr "For at alle arbejderknuder skal være i den samme serverfarm, skal de pege på den samme database."

#: ../../index.rst:108
msgid "3. Storage Component"
msgstr "3. Lagerkomponent"

#: ../../index.rst:110
msgid ""
"The storage component is the persistent storage location for files and "
"folders. There are two different types of storage services. One is "
"managed by CentreStack, such as the default storage for the cluster and "
"the default storage for tenants. The other is imported storage, for "
"example, having existing file server network shares that aren't managed "
"by CentreStack but can be imported into CentreStack for remote and mobile"
" access."
msgstr "Lagringskomponenten er det vedvarende lagringssted for filer og mapper. Der er to forskellige typer af lagringstjenester. Den ene administreres af CentreStack, såsom standardlagringen for klyngen og standardlagringen for lejere. Den anden er importeret lagring, for eksempel at have eksisterende filservernetværksdelinger, der ikke administreres af CentreStack, men som kan importeres til CentreStack for fjern- og mobiladgang."

#: ../../index.rst:117
msgid "Terminology"
msgstr ""

#: ../../index.rst:120
msgid "CentreStack Partner Portal"
msgstr "CentreStack Partner Portal"

#: ../../index.rst:122
msgid ""
"The Partner Portal can be found by going to http://www.centrestack.com. "
"Click on \"Partner\" to sign up for your partner account log in "
"credentials, and then you can log into your partner account at anytime. "
"From the Partner Portal, You are able to download the CentreStack "
"software and can start the trial process. Later, you can acquire licenses"
" to turn the trial into a production environment."
msgstr "Partnerportalen kan findes ved at gå til http://www.centrestack.com. Klik på \"Partner\" for at tilmelde dig dine partnerkonto loginoplysninger, og derefter kan du logge ind på din partnerkonto når som helst. Fra Partnerportalen kan du downloade CentreStack-softwaren og kan starte prøveprocessen. Senere kan du erhverve licenser til at omdanne prøven til et produktionsmiljø."

#: ../../index.rst:128
msgid "You can manage hosted-tenants from the partner portal."
msgstr "Du kan administrere hosted-tenants fra partnerportalen."

#: ../../index.rst:130
msgid ""
"You can also come back to the partner portal any time that your "
"CentreStack software needs to be upgraded to a later version."
msgstr "Du kan også vende tilbage til partnerportalen når som helst, når din CentreStack-software skal opgraderes til en nyere version."

#: ../../index.rst:134
msgid "CentreStack Cluster - Server Farm"
msgstr "CentreStack Cluster - Servergård"

#: ../../index.rst:136
msgid ""
"Multiple CentreStack single-machine nodes connect together by pointing to"
" the same database and then share the same configuration information from"
" the database so that CentreStack can indirectly share the persistent "
"storage location in a symmetrical way."
msgstr "Flere CentreStack enkeltmaskine-noder forbinder sammen ved at pege på den samme database og derefter dele de samme konfigurationsoplysninger fra databasen, så CentreStack indirekte kan dele den vedvarende lagringsplacering på en symmetrisk måde."

#: ../../index.rst:138
msgid ""
"Indirectly, the database contains storage related information so all the "
"nodes in the server farm share storage related configuration."
msgstr "Indirekte indeholder databasen oplysninger relateret til lagring, så alle noderne i serverfarmen deler konfiguration relateret til lagring."

#: ../../index.rst:141
msgid ""
"The whole CentreStack cluster operates as if it is a single entity. The "
"smallest cluster is a single CentreStack worker node, which contains all "
"the functionality and different logical nodes together."
msgstr "Hele CentreStack-klusteret fungerer, som om det er en enkelt enhed. Det mindste kluster er en enkelt CentreStack-arbejderknode, som indeholder al funktionaliteten og forskellige logiske noder sammen."

#: ../../index.rst:144
msgid "Another term for the cluster is the **CentreStack server farm**."
msgstr "Et andet udtryk for klyngen er **CentreStack serverfarmen**."

#: ../../index.rst:148
msgid "The smallest cluster can be a single all-in-one worker node."
msgstr "Den mindste klynge kan være en enkelt alt-i-én arbejdsnode."

#: ../../index.rst:151
msgid "Master Admin/Cluster Admin"
msgstr "Masteradministrator/Clusteradministrator"

#: ../../index.rst:153
msgid ""
"In this guide, we refer to the admin user as the user that manages the "
"whole CentreStack server farm. The server farm can be as small as a "
"single CentreStack server. If so, the admin user will still need to "
"manage it regardless of the size of the server farm."
msgstr "I denne vejledning henviser vi til administratoren som den bruger, der administrerer hele CentreStack serverfarmen. Serverfarmen kan være så lille som en enkelt CentreStack server. Hvis det er tilfældet, skal administratoren stadig administrere den uanset størrelsen på serverfarmen."

#: ../../index.rst:158
msgid ""
"The Master Admin is the very first user on the CentreStack server farm. "
"Typically, it is the user who installs the CentreStack server software."
msgstr "Masteradministratoren er den allerførste bruger på CentreStack-serverfarmen. Det er typisk den bruger, der installerer CentreStack-serversoftwaren."

#: ../../index.rst:161
msgid ""
"Since this user later may set up optional Active Directory connections, "
"it is recommended that this user's email address is not from the same "
"Active Directory to avoid circular dependency."
msgstr "Da denne bruger senere kan opsætte valgfrie Active Directory-forbindelser, anbefales det, at denne brugers e-mailadresse ikke er fra samme Active Directory for at undgå cirkulær afhængighed."

#: ../../index.rst:165
msgid "Tenant"
msgstr "Lejer"

#: ../../index.rst:167
msgid ""
"CentreStack is a multi-tenant ready solution. A tenant here usually is "
"mapped to:"
msgstr "CentreStack er en løsning klar til flere lejere. En lejer her er normalt kortlagt til:"

#: ../../index.rst:170
msgid "a company (if you are the company IT)"
msgstr "en virksomhed (hvis du er virksomhedens IT)"

#: ../../index.rst:171
msgid "a client of yours (if you are a Managed Service Provider/MSP)"
msgstr "en klient af din (hvis du er en Managed Service Provider/MSP)"

#: ../../index.rst:173
msgid "Tenants are created by the cluster administrator."
msgstr "Lejere oprettes af klyngeadministratoren."

#: ../../index.rst:175
msgid ""
"You can use the CentreStack server in a single tenant setup because it is"
" just a special case of multi-tenancy."
msgstr "Du kan bruge CentreStack-serveren i en enkelt lejeropsætning, fordi det blot er et specielt tilfælde af multi-tenancy."

#: ../../index.rst:179
msgid ""
"From a reporting perspective, a tenant contains a number of users and "
"also storage quota and storage consumption."
msgstr "Fra et rapporteringssynspunkt indeholder en tenant et antal brugere samt lagerkvote og lagerforbrug."

#: ../../index.rst:182
msgid ""
"From the technical side, a tenant is usually connected to an Active "
"Directory and can have a bunch of connected file servers either directly "
"or through server agents."
msgstr "Fra det tekniske perspektiv er en tenant normalt forbundet til en Active Directory og kan have en række forbundne filservere enten direkte eller gennem serveragenter."

#: ../../index.rst:186
msgid "Tenant Admin"
msgstr "Lejeradministrator"

#: ../../index.rst:188
msgid ""
"These are the users who actually use the product but are the admins for "
"their teams (tenant or company)."
msgstr "Disse er brugerne, som faktisk bruger produktet, men er administratorer for deres hold (lejer eller firma)."

#: ../../index.rst:190
msgid ""
"This is the very first tenant account user. Usually, the Tenant User is "
"created by Master Admin."
msgstr "Dette er den allerførste brugerkonto for lejer. Normalt oprettes lejerbrugeren af hovedadministratoren."

#: ../../index.rst:192
msgid ""
"The Master Admin is also the Tenant Admin for his own team/company "
"(default tenant). Tenant admin can later delegate administrative tasks to"
" other team users."
msgstr "Masteradministratoren er også Tenant Admin for sit eget hold/sin egen virksomhed (standardlejer). Tenant-administratoren kan senere delegere administrative opgaver til andre teambrugere."

#: ../../index.rst:194
msgid ""
"By default the cluster administrator can help the tenant administrator on"
" the management scope."
msgstr "Som standard kan klyngeadministratoren hjælpe lejeradministratoren med administrationsomfanget."

#: ../../index.rst:197
msgid "Tenant User"
msgstr "Lejerbruger"

#: ../../index.rst:199
msgid ""
"The tenant user (team user) is a user inside a specific Tenant.  Team "
"users are created by the Tenant Admin (or by cluster admin on behalf of "
"the tenant admin). Team users can come from four different places:"
msgstr "Lejerbrugeren (teambruger) er en bruger inden for en specifik lejer. Teambrugere oprettes af lejeradministratoren (eller af klyngeadministratoren på vegne af lejeradministratoren). Teambrugere kan komme fra fire forskellige steder:"

#: ../../index.rst:201
msgid "Native CentreStack User (created from scratch)"
msgstr "Indfødt CentreStack-bruger (oprettet fra bunden)"

#: ../../index.rst:202
msgid "Active Directory User from local LDAP"
msgstr "Active Directory-bruger fra lokal LDAP"

#: ../../index.rst:203
msgid "Active Directory User from remote CentreStack Server Agent"
msgstr "Active Directory-bruger fra fjern CentreStack Server Agent"

#: ../../index.rst:204
msgid "Azure AD or other single-sign-on integrated identity provider"
msgstr "Azure AD eller anden single-sign-on integreret identitetsudbyder"

#: ../../index.rst:206
msgid ""
"Team users always belong to a specific tenant and can't span multiple "
"tenants. However, a team user can receive file and folder share from "
"multiple users and from multiple tenants."
msgstr "Teambrugere tilhører altid en specifik lejer og kan ikke spænde over flere lejere. Dog kan en teambruger modtage fil- og mappeaktier fra flere brugere og fra flere lejere."

#: ../../index.rst:212
msgid ""
"A Native CentreStack user can be mapped to Active Directory user or Azure"
" AD user later if necessary."
msgstr "En Native CentreStack-bruger kan efter behov mappes til en Active Directory-bruger eller Azure AD-bruger senere."

#: ../../index.rst:216
msgid "Guest User"
msgstr "Gæstebruger"

#: ../../index.rst:218
msgid ""
"The guest users are users outside of the tenant users domain but receive "
"file or folder shares from team user. The Team user creates guest users "
"through the file sharing or folder sharing activities. Guest users "
"typically are external users outside of an organization that are already "
"using CentreStack."
msgstr "Gæstebrugere er brugere uden for lejerbrugerens domæne, men modtager fildelinger eller mappeaktier fra teambrugeren. Teambrugeren opretter gæstebrugere gennem aktiviteter for fildeling eller mappeaktier. Gæstebrugere er typisk eksterne brugere uden for en organisation, der allerede bruger CentreStack."

#: ../../index.rst:223
msgid "Anonymous User"
msgstr "Anonym bruger"

#: ../../index.rst:225
msgid ""
"The anonymous users are a type of the guest user that doesn't require "
"editing permission. They can receive files and folder shares and can view"
" the file and folder share from within a web browser user interface."
msgstr "Anonyme brugere er en type gæstebruger, der ikke kræver redigeringstilladelse. De kan modtage filer og mappeandele og kan se fil- og mappeandelen fra et webbrowser-brugergrænseflade."

#: ../../index.rst:229
msgid "Client Agent Software"
msgstr "Klient Agent Software"

#: ../../index.rst:231
msgid "CentreStack contains various client agents which include:"
msgstr "CentreStack indeholder forskellige klientagenter, som inkluderer:"

#: ../../index.rst:233
msgid "Web Browser Based File Manager"
msgstr "Webbrowserbaseret Filhåndtering"

#: ../../index.rst:234
msgid "Windows Desktop Client with Mapped Drive"
msgstr "Windows Desktop-klient med tilknyttet drev"

#: ../../index.rst:235
msgid "Windows File Server Agent with 2-way synchronization"
msgstr "Windows-filserveragent med 2-vejs synkronisering"

#: ../../index.rst:236
msgid "Mac OS X client and"
msgstr "Mac OS X-klient og"

#: ../../index.rst:240
msgid "Mobile Applications:"
msgstr "Mobilapplikationer:"

#: ../../index.rst:238
msgid "iOS"
msgstr "iOS"

#: ../../index.rst:239
msgid "Android"
msgstr "Android"

#: ../../index.rst:240
msgid "Windows Phone"
msgstr "Windows Phone"

#: ../../index.rst:242
msgid ""
"These client agents provide file access and sharing features from the "
"native client operating systems."
msgstr "Disse klientagenter giver adgang til filer og delingsfunktioner fra de oprindelige klientoperativsystemer."

#: ../../index.rst:245
msgid ""
"The discussion of the client agents are outside the scope of this "
"deployment guide."
msgstr "Diskussionen om klientagenterne ligger uden for rammerne af denne installationsguide."

#: ../../index.rst:248
msgid "System Requirements"
msgstr "Systemkrav"

#: ../../index.rst:250
msgid ""
"CentreStack server is built on top of the Microsoft Web Platform, which "
"includes:"
msgstr "CentreStack-serveren er bygget på toppen af Microsofts webplatform, som inkluderer:"

#: ../../index.rst:252
msgid "Windows Server base operating system"
msgstr "Windows Server basisoperativsystem"

#: ../../index.rst:253
msgid "Internet Information Server 7/8/10 (IIS)"
msgstr "Internet Information Server 7/8/10 (IIS)"

#: ../../index.rst:254
msgid ".Net Framework 4.5+"
msgstr ".Net Framework 4.5+"

#: ../../index.rst:255
msgid "ASP.NET"
msgstr "ASP.NET"

#: ../../index.rst:256
msgid "MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server or Microsoft SQL Server Express"
msgstr "MySQL, Microsoft SQL Server eller Microsoft SQL Server Express"

#: ../../index.rst:258
msgid "The base operating system can be either:"
msgstr "Basisoperativsystemet kan være enten:"

#: ../../index.rst:260
msgid "Windows Server 2025"
msgstr "Windows Server 2025"

#: ../../index.rst:261
msgid "Windows Server 2022"
msgstr "Windows Server 2022"

#: ../../index.rst:262
msgid "Windows Server 2019"
msgstr "Windows Server 2019"

#: ../../index.rst:264
msgid ""
"We recommend Windows Server 2025/2022/2019 since .Net Framework 4.5+ "
"comes directly with these newer server OS platforms. It is easier and "
"faster to install CentreStack software on Windows Server 2025/2022/2019."
msgstr "Vi anbefaler Windows Server 2025/2022/2019, da .Net Framework 4.5+ følger direkte med disse nyere server OS platforme. Det er nemmere og hurtigere at installere CentreStack software på Windows Server 2025/2022/2019."

#: ../../index.rst:269
msgid ""
"The CentreStack server installer is capable of installing all the "
"dependency system components such as .NET Framework and etc. For "
"installation, a clean machine is recommended."
msgstr "CentreStack serverinstallatøren er i stand til at installere alle afhængige systemkomponenter såsom .NET Framework og lignende. Til installation anbefales en ren maskine."

#: ../../index.rst:271
msgid ""
"There is no need to prepare the machine beyond the clean state of the "
"basic Operating System software."
msgstr "Der er ikke behov for at forberede maskinen ud over den rene tilstand af den grundlæggende operativsystemsoftware."

#: ../../index.rst:275
msgid "Windows Server 2025, 2022, 2019"
msgstr "Windows Server 2025, 2022, 2019"

#: ../../index.rst:277
msgid ""
"The base operating system provides the base of the Microsoft Web "
"Platform. It will be loaded with the mentioned Microsoft components "
"before the core CentreStack software is installed."
msgstr "Det grundlæggende operativsystem udgør basen for Microsofts webplatform. Det vil blive indlæst med de nævnte Microsoft-komponenter, før den centrale CentreStack-software installeres."

#: ../../index.rst:281
msgid ""
"The CentreStack installer will install and load  all the dependency "
"Windows components."
msgstr "CentreStack-installationsprogrammet vil installere og indlæse alle de afhængige Windows-komponenter."

#: ../../index.rst:285
msgid ""
"Base Operating System with English locale is recommended. (The User "
"Interface can be in a different locale.)"
msgstr "Det anbefales at bruge et grundlæggende operativsystem med engelsk landestandard. (Brugergrænsefladen kan være på et andet sprog.)"

#: ../../index.rst:288
msgid "SQL Server / MySQL Server"
msgstr "SQL Server / MySQL Server"

#: ../../index.rst:290
msgid ""
"The Microsoft SQL Server or SQL Server Express or MySQL is used to store "
"static configuration information such as the user name, email, storage "
"configuration, files and folders, sharing information and others."
msgstr "Microsoft SQL Server eller SQL Server Express eller MySQL bruges til at gemme statiske konfigurationsoplysninger såsom brugernavn, e-mail, lagerkonfiguration, filer og mapper, delingsoplysninger og andet."

#: ../../index.rst:293
msgid ""
"It is recommended that the SQL Server has daily backups since it contains"
" configuration information for the service to run properly."
msgstr "Det anbefales, at SQL-serveren har daglige sikkerhedskopier, da den indeholder konfigurationsoplysninger for, at tjenesten kan køre korrekt."

#: ../../index.rst:295
msgid ""
"If you have SQL Server Standard Edition or SQL Server Enterprise Edition,"
" you can take advantage of the high availability features like Always-On "
"Clustering or Always-On Fail Over Group."
msgstr "Hvis du har SQL Server Standard Edition eller SQL Server Enterprise Edition, kan du drage fordel af funktionerne til høj tilgængelighed som Always-On Clustering eller Always-On Fail Over Group."

#: ../../index.rst:298
msgid "MySQL Community Edition is also supported."
msgstr "MySQL Community Edition understøttes også."

#: ../../index.rst:300
msgid ""
"If you are setting CentreStack server up in Amazon AWS, Amazon Aurora DB "
"is also recommended."
msgstr "Hvis du opsætter en CentreStack-server i Amazon AWS, anbefales det også at bruge Amazon Aurora DB."

#: ../../index.rst:304
msgid ""
"The CentreStack server installer is capable of installing SQL Express or "
"MySQL. If you only need an all-in-one deployment for a single server "
"deployment, the installer can install the database automatically."
msgstr "CentreStack serverinstallatøren er i stand til at installere SQL Express eller MySQL. Hvis du kun har brug for en alt-i-én-udrulning til en enkelt serverudrulning, kan installatøren installere databasen automatisk."

#: ../../index.rst:307
msgid ".Net Framework 4"
msgstr ".Net Framework 4"

#: ../../index.rst:309
msgid ""
"The CentreStack Server is built with .Net Framework 4, with ASP.NET and "
"WCF."
msgstr "CentreStack-serveren er bygget med .Net Framework 4, med ASP.NET og WCF."

#: ../../index.rst:311
msgid ""
"We recommend .Net Framework 4.5 and above as it works better with remote "
"clients that have Internet Explorer 10 or 11."
msgstr "Vi anbefaler .Net Framework 4.5 og nyere, da det fungerer bedre med fjernklienter, der har Internet Explorer 10 eller 11."

#: ../../index.rst:315
msgid ""
"The CentreStack server Installer will install .NET 4.5 and other "
"dependency components automatically."
msgstr "CentreStack server-installationsprogrammet vil automatisk installere .NET 4.5 og andre afhængighedskomponenter."

#: ../../index.rst:319
msgid "ASP.NET 4.5/4.6/4.7"
msgstr "ASP.NET 4.5/4.6/4.7"

#: ../../index.rst:321
msgid ""
"CentreStack web browser portal user interface is written in ASP.NET, HTML"
" and JavaScript."
msgstr "CentreStacks webbrowserportal brugergrænseflade er skrevet i ASP.NET, HTML og JavaScript."

#: ../../index.rst:324
msgid "Internet Information Server (IIS)"
msgstr "Internetinformationsserver (IIS)"

#: ../../index.rst:326
msgid ""
"CentreStack Server-side services are hosted inside the Internet "
"Information Server (IIS). It provides brokerage functionalities and "
"secure gateway between the Client Agents and the back-end storage. It is "
"also a value-add layer on top of the back-end storage."
msgstr "CentreStack-serverens tjenester er hostet inde i Internet Information Server (IIS). Det leverer mæglerfunktioner og sikker gateway mellem klientagenterne og backend-lagringen. Det er også et værditilføjende lag oven på backend-lagringen."

#: ../../index.rst:332
msgid ""
"The CentreStack Server Installer will enable IIS Service if not already. "
"So no manual step required."
msgstr "CentreStack Server Installer vil aktivere IIS-tjenesten, hvis den ikke allerede er det. Så intet manuelt skridt er nødvendigt."

#: ../../index.rst:335
msgid "Recommended Hardware Specification"
msgstr "Anbefalet hardware specifikation"

#: ../../index.rst
msgid "Memory"
msgstr "Hukommelse"

#: ../../index.rst:339
msgid "4GB, (8+GB is better for production environment)"
msgstr "4GB, (8+GB er bedre til produktionsmiljø)"

#: ../../index.rst
msgid "Hard Drive"
msgstr "Harddisk"

#: ../../index.rst:343
msgid "100G"
msgstr "100G"

#: ../../index.rst
msgid "Operating System"
msgstr "Operativsystem"

#: ../../index.rst:347
msgid "Windows Server 2025, Windows Server 2022, Windows Server 2019"
msgstr "Windows Server 2025, Windows Server 2022, Windows Server 2019"

#: ../../index.rst
msgid "CPU"
msgstr "CPU"

#: ../../index.rst:351
msgid ""
"Intel, minimum 2-Core, prefer 4-Core (or 2-vCPU/4-vCPU  if on a virtual "
"machine)"
msgstr "Intel, minimum 2-Core, foretrækker 4-Core (eller 2-vCPU/4-vCPU hvis på en virtuel maskine)"

#: ../../index.rst:355
msgid ""
"Virtual Machines are recommended. A Clean machine built from a base OS "
"with English Locale is recommended. After providing the clean machine, "
"the CentreStack Server installer will install the rest of the Windows "
"system components and CentreStack components automatically. The software "
"is hypervisor neutral. The hypervisor can be Hyper-V, VMWare or others. "
"The software can be installed on a physical machine as well if needed."
msgstr "Virtuelle maskiner anbefales. En ren maskine bygget fra et grundlæggende OS med engelsk landestandard anbefales. Efter at have leveret den rene maskine, vil CentreStack Server-installationsprogrammet automatisk installere resten af Windows-systemkomponenterne og CentreStack-komponenterne. Softwaren er hypervisor-neutral. Hypervisoren kan være Hyper-V, VMWare eller andre. Softwaren kan også installeres på en fysisk maskine, hvis det er nødvendigt."

#: ../../index.rst:361
msgid "Capacity Planning"
msgstr "Kapacitetsplanlægning"

#: ../../index.rst:363
msgid ""
"For user counts smaller than 1000, a single CentreStack server is enough."
" Most of the time, an all-in-one server deployment will be sufficient. In"
" this case you will install the CentreStack Server in a single physical "
"or virtual machine. The default CentreStack installer will install all "
"the components (Database/Web Node/Worker Node) on one machine."
msgstr "For brugerantal mindre end 1000 er en enkelt CentreStack-server tilstrækkelig. Det meste af tiden vil en alt-i-én serverinstallation være tilstrækkelig. I dette tilfælde vil du installere CentreStack-serveren på en enkelt fysisk eller virtuel maskine. Den standard CentreStack-installer vil installere alle komponenterne (Database/Web Node/Worker Node) på én maskine."

#: ../../index.rst:366
msgid ""
"For user counts greater than 1000, it is recommended to have the SQL "
"Server node in a separate physical or virtual machine."
msgstr "For brugerantal større end 1000 anbefales det at have SQL Server-noden på en separat fysisk eller virtuel maskine."

#: ../../index.rst:368
msgid ""
"The rest of the worker nodes will share the load for the users in a "
"capacity of 1000 each."
msgstr "De resterende arbejderknuder vil dele belastningen for brugerne med en kapacitet på 1000 hver."

#: ../../index.rst:370
msgid ""
"In this case a virtual machine is recommended for each worker node and "
"you should use a wild card SSL certificate for each worker node."
msgstr "I dette tilfælde anbefales en virtuel maskine for hver arbejderknode, og du bør bruge et wildcard SSL-certifikat for hver arbejderknode."

#: ../../index.rst:374
msgid ""
"In some big deployments, the SSL can be off-loaded to hardware load "
"balancer such as Citrix NetScaler or F5 BIG IP."
msgstr "I nogle store udrulninger kan SSL aflastes til hardware load balancer som Citrix NetScaler eller F5 BIG IP."

#: ../../index.rst:376
msgid ""
"The capacity of 1000 is referring to concurrent users. It is possible "
"that you may have 5000 named users but only 1000 of them are using the "
"product concurrently. So, in this case the per-server capacity can be "
"5000 named users."
msgstr "Kapaciteten på 1000 henviser til samtidige brugere. Det er muligt, at du kan have 5000 navngivne brugere, men kun 1000 af dem bruger produktet samtidigt. Så i dette tilfælde kan kapaciteten pr. server være 5000 navngivne brugere."

#: ../../index.rst:382
msgid ""
"(A Concurrent-User is defined as the users making requests in a 10-second"
" period. For example, if you make a request A, and I make a request B, "
"and if the time-difference between request A and request B is less than "
"10 seconds, request A and request B are concurrent)."
msgstr "(En Samtidig-Bruger defineres som brugere, der foretager anmodninger inden for et 10-sekunders interval. For eksempel, hvis du foretager en anmodning A, og jeg foretager en anmodning B, og tidsforskellen mellem anmodning A og anmodning B er mindre end 10 sekunder, er anmodning A og anmodning B samtidige)."

#: ../../index.rst:386
msgid ""
"**EXAMPLE**\\:  If you have 300,000 users in your company, you may need "
"between 30-60 worker nodes (5000 – 10,000 named users for each worker "
"node). You can scale up the memory size for each worker node to reduce "
"the number of worker nodes required."
msgstr "**EKSEMPEL**\: Hvis du har 300.000 brugere i din virksomhed, kan du få brug for mellem 30-60 arbejderknuder (5000 – 10.000 navngivne brugere for hver arbejderknude). Du kan skalere hukommelsesstørrelsen for hver arbejderknude for at reducere antallet af nødvendige arbejderknuder."

#: ../../index.rst:390
msgid "Load Balancing"
msgstr "Loadbalancering"

#: ../../index.rst:392
msgid ""
"Our recommendation is to have your own load balancing device if possible."
" However, CentreStack is capable of using worker nodes (for web function "
"only) for load-balancing if you do not have an existing load balancer. "
"You can pick a worker node to be the node exposed for login/contact point"
" and pass the actual work to others."
msgstr "Vores anbefaling er at have din egen load balancing-enhed, hvis det er muligt. CentreStack er dog i stand til at bruge arbejderknuder (kun til webfunktion) til load-balancing, hvis du ikke har en eksisterende load balancer. Du kan vælge en arbejderknude til at være den knude, der er udsat for login/kontaktpunkt og overdrage det egentlige arbejde til andre."

#: ../../index.rst:396
msgid ""
"If you have a hardware load balancer such as F5, you can skip web nodes, "
"and have F5 directly load balance to a farm of worker nodes. You can also"
" use the Network Load Balancing feature which is included in Windows Server "
"2025/2022/2019 for load balancing."
msgstr "Hvis du har en hardware load balancer som F5, kan du springe webknuderne over og lade F5 direkte balancere belastningen til en gruppe af arbejderknuder. Du kan også bruge Network Load Balancing-funktionen, som er inkluderet i Windows Server 2025/2022/2019 til load balancing."

#: ../../index.rst:401
msgid "Active Directory Integration"
msgstr "Active Directory-integration"

#: ../../index.rst:403
msgid "There are three ways to connect Active Directory into CentreStack."
msgstr "Der er tre måder at forbinde Active Directory med CentreStack på."

#: ../../index.rst:407
msgid "1. LDAP"
msgstr "LDAP"

#: ../../index.rst:409
msgid ""
"For the first way, if the Active Directory is in the same Local Area "
"Network (LAN), then a direct LDAP/LDAPS connection is recommended."
msgstr "For den første metode, hvis Active Directory er i det samme lokale område netværk (LAN), så anbefales en direkte LDAP/LDAPS forbindelse."

#: ../../index.rst:414
msgid "2. Server Agent Proxy"
msgstr "2. Serveragentproxy"

#: ../../index.rst:416
msgid ""
"For the Second way, if the Active Directory is in a remote office, such "
"as on a customer's premise, away from the CentreStack server, then a "
"client agent software called, \"File Server Agent\" can be installed on "
"the remote file server to help import Active Directory users over to "
"CentreStack."
msgstr "For det andet, hvis Active Directory befinder sig på et eksternt kontor, såsom hos en kunde, væk fra CentreStack-serveren, kan en klientagent-software kaldet \"File Server Agent\" installeres på den eksterne filserver for at hjælpe med at importere Active Directory-brugere over til CentreStack."

#: ../../index.rst:422
msgid "CentreStack allows you to connect to multiple active directory services."
msgstr "CentreStack giver dig mulighed for at forbinde til flere active directory-tjenester."

#: ../../index.rst:425
msgid "3. Azure AD Support"
msgstr "3. Azure AD Support"

#: ../../index.rst:426
msgid ""
"Via the Azure AD support, you can setup Azure AD so users can be "
"authenticated by Azure AD instead of from a local Active Directory."
msgstr "Via Azure AD-supporten kan du opsætte Azure AD, så brugere kan blive godkendt af Azure AD i stedet for fra en lokal Active Directory."

#: ../../index.rst:430
msgid "**\"Proxied AD User\"**"
msgstr "**\"Proxied AD-bruger\"**"

#: ../../index.rst:432
msgid ""
"It is also possible to use the Active Directory from a remote location "
"where the server agent (included client software) is used. In this case "
"\"Proxied AD User\" will be referred to users imported from server "
"agent's side of the Active Directory."
msgstr "Det er også muligt at bruge Active Directory fra en fjern placering, hvor serveragenten (inkluderet klientsoftware) anvendes. I dette tilfælde vil \"Proxied AD User\" referere til brugere importeret fra serveragentens side af Active Directory."

#: ../../index.rst:435
msgid "**\"AD User\"**"
msgstr "**\"AD Bruger\"**"

#: ../../index.rst:437
msgid ""
"The \"AD user\" is reserved to refer to users from local LDAP Active "
"Directory."
msgstr "Begrebet \"AD bruger\" er forbeholdt brugere fra lokal LDAP Active Directory."

#: ../../index.rst:442
msgid ""
"When should you use LDAP, and when should you use \"Server Agent\" for AD"
" integration?"
msgstr "Hvornår skal du bruge LDAP, og hvornår skal du bruge \"Server Agent\" til AD-integration?"

#: ../../index.rst:444
msgid "If AD is local to the CentreStack server, then LDAP is recommended."
msgstr "Hvis AD er lokal til CentreStack-serveren, anbefales LDAP."

#: ../../index.rst:446
msgid "If AD is remote, then Server Agent is recommended."
msgstr "Hvis AD er fjern, anbefales Server Agent."

#: ../../index.rst:450
msgid "Storage Considerations"
msgstr "Lagringsbetraktninger"

#: ../../index.rst:452
msgid ""
"In the CentreStack system, for each tenant, there is one mandatory "
"primary storage and there can be multiple, optional auxiliary storage "
"services. The primary storage is the tenant's default root storage "
"folder."
msgstr "I CentreStack-systemet er der for hver lejer én obligatorisk primær opbevaring og der kan være flere valgfrie hjælpeopbevaringstjenester. Den primære opbevaring er lejerens standard rodmappe til opbevaring."

#: ../../index.rst:455
msgid ""
"If you setup the CentreStack in Amazon EC2 environment, the primary "
"storage usually is an Amazon S3 bucket."
msgstr "Hvis du opsætter CentreStack i Amazon EC2-miljøet, er det primære lager som regel en Amazon S3-bucket."

#: ../../index.rst:457
msgid ""
"If you setup the CentreStack on-premise, the primary storage can be your "
"file server storage and the auxiliary storage can be other cloud storage "
"services or other local file server storage. OpenStack Swift is also a "
"popular storage service in private enterprises."
msgstr "Hvis du opsætter CentreStack on-premise, kan primær opbevaring være din filserveropbevaring, og sekundær opbevaring kan være andre cloudopbevaringstjenester eller anden lokal filserveropbevaring. OpenStack Swift er også en populær opbevaringstjeneste i private virksomheder."

#: ../../index.rst:460
msgid ""
"CentreStack can be setup in a Rackspace data center on Cloud Server, "
"Windows Azure VM, IBM SoftLayer Data Center and connect to Cloud Files, "
"Azure Blob Storage, and SoftLayer Object Storage (OpenStack Swift based) "
"respectively."
msgstr "CentreStack kan opsættes i et Rackspace-datacenter på Cloud Server, Windows Azure VM, IBM SoftLayer Data Center og forbinde til Cloud Files, Azure Blob Storage og SoftLayer Object Storage (baseret på OpenStack Swift) henholdsvis."

#: ../../index.rst:463
msgid ""
"CentreStack can also be setup next to a File Server and connect directly "
"to a File Server Network Share."
msgstr "CentreStack kan også opsættes ved siden af en filserver og forbindes direkte til et netværksdeling på en filserver."

#: ../../index.rst:467
msgid ""
"If you will later have multiple CentreStack worker nodes in the cluster, "
"make sure you use storage service connector in a way that can be accessed"
" from all of the worker nodes."
msgstr "Hvis du senere vil have flere CentreStack arbejderknuder i klyngen, skal du sørge for at bruge lagringstjenestekonnektoren på en måde, så den kan tilgås fra alle arbejderknuderne."

#: ../../index.rst:470
msgid ""
"For example, C:\\\\ Drive of a specific worker node is not a good one to "
"be accessed from all worker nodes. However, if it is published as a "
"network share, it is good for all worker nodes."
msgstr "For eksempel er C:\\ drevet af en specifik arbejdsnode ikke godt at få adgang til fra alle arbejdsnoder. Men hvis det offentliggøres som et netværksdrev, er det godt for alle arbejdsnoder."

#: ../../index.rst:474
msgid "Backup CentreStack"
msgstr "Backup CentreStack"

#: ../../index.rst:477
msgid "Database"
msgstr "Database"

#: ../../index.rst:479
msgid ""
"Only the CentreStack database contains persistent configuration "
"information. All other components are stateless and replaceable. In a "
"disaster recovery scenario, as soon as the SQL Server is restored, other "
"worker nodes can be re-installed and will start working immediately. You "
"can also point the worker node's database reference to the new SQL "
"Server; it will work immediately with the information from the database."
msgstr "Kun CentreStack-databasen indeholder vedvarende konfigurationsinformation. Alle andre komponenter er tilstandsløse og kan udskiftes. I et katastrofegenoprettelsesscenarie vil andre arbejdsnoder kunne geninstalleres og begynde at arbejde med det samme, så snart SQL Server er gendannet. Du kan også pege arbejdsnodens databasehenvisning til den nye SQL Server; den vil straks fungere med oplysningerne fra databasen."

#: ../../index.rst:486
msgid ""
"The worker nodes are stateless so it is not required to backup any worker"
" nodes. They can be provisioned by a clean OS with a copy of CentreStack."
" As soon as they are connected to the same database they become a node in"
" the cluster."
msgstr "Arbejderknuderne er tilstandsløse, så det er ikke nødvendigt at tage backup af nogen arbejderknuder. De kan blive klargjort af et rent operativsystem med en kopi af CentreStack. Så snart de er forbundet til den samme database, bliver de en knude i klyngen."

#: ../../index.rst:491
msgid "Storage (Files and Folders)"
msgstr "Lagring (Filer og Mapper)"

#: ../../index.rst:493
msgid ""
"You will also need to back up your storage services. Most of the time, if"
" you are using Cloud Storage services such as Amazon S3 or OpenStack "
"Swift, the service has built-in redundancy. For local storage, DFS "
"replication, RAID array or Microsoft Storage Space can all be options to "
"provide storage service redundancy."
msgstr "Du skal også sikre backup af dine lagringstjenester. Størstedelen af tiden, hvis du bruger Cloud Storage-tjenester som Amazon S3 eller OpenStack Swift, har tjenesten indbygget redundans. For lokal lagring kan DFS-replikering, RAID-array eller Microsoft Storage Space alle være muligheder for at tilvejebringe redundans i lagringstjenesten."

#: ../../index.rst:498
msgid "Deployment Scenarios"
msgstr "Udrulningsscenarier"

#: ../../index.rst:501
msgid "Private On-premise"
msgstr "Privat On-premise"

#: ../../index.rst:503
msgid ""
"You can prepare a Windows Server 2025/2022/2019 and install CentreStack. "
"In this scenario, Active Directory is typically at the same site and "
"primary storage is from file server or NAS storage."
msgstr "Du kan forberede en Windows Server 2025/2022/2019 og installere CentreStack. I dette scenarie er Active Directory typisk på samme sted, og primær opbevaring er fra filserver eller NAS-opbevaring."

#: ../../index.rst:506
msgid ""
"In this case, most of the time you are using CentreStack as a way to "
"replace VPN to provide access to onsite file server from mobile devices "
"and remote devices."
msgstr "I de fleste tilfælde bruger du CentreStack som en måde at erstatte VPN for at give adgang til filserver på stedet fra mobile enheder og fjernenheder."

#: ../../index.rst:511
msgid ""
"Business Access use case - provide access to file server via CentreStack "
"to mobile devices. When employees are in the office, they access the file"
" server their normal way without noticing any difference, and while on "
"the road or from remote location, they can use mobile and remote device "
"to access file server network shares."
msgstr "Business Access-brugssag - giver adgang til filserver via CentreStack til mobile enheder. Når medarbejdere er på kontoret, tilgår de filserveren på deres sædvanlige måde uden at bemærke nogen forskel, og mens de er på farten eller fra en fjern lokation, kan de bruge mobile og fjernenheder til at få adgang til filserverens netværksdelinger."

#: ../../index.rst:521
msgid "Private Off-Premise"
msgstr "Privat Off-Premise"

#: ../../index.rst:523
msgid ""
"Normally, a managed service provider (MSP) manages your IT services, such"
" as hosted exchange servers, hosted file servers etc. You can ask the "
"same managed service provider to install and manage the CentreStack for "
"you in their data center."
msgstr "Normalt administrerer en managed service provider (MSP) dine IT-tjenester, såsom hosted exchange servere, hosted file servere osv. Du kan bede den samme managed service provider om at installere og administrere CentreStack for dig i deres datacenter."

#: ../../index.rst:526
msgid ""
"Usually from this deployment scenario, if the file server is already in "
"the same data center, typically it turned into the \"Private On-premise\""
" deployment."
msgstr "Normalt fra dette udrulningsscenarie, hvis filserveren allerede er i samme datacenter, bliver den typisk omdannet til \"Privat On-premise\" udrulning."

#: ../../index.rst:529
msgid ""
"If on the other hand, the file servers are away from the data center, "
"this gets turned into \"Business Continuity\" use case, where the server "
"agent can be installed on the local file server and connects the local "
"file servers to the remote CentreStack server in the data center."
msgstr "Hvis filserverne derimod er væk fra datacentret, bliver dette omdannet til et \"Business Continuity\"-anvendelsestilfælde, hvor serveragenten kan installeres på den lokale filserver og forbinde de lokale filservere til den fjernbetjente CentreStack-server i datacentret."

#: ../../index.rst:535
msgid "Virtual Private Cloud"
msgstr "Virtuel Privat Sky"

#: ../../index.rst:537
msgid ""
"In this deployment scenario, you would deploy the CentreStack solution in"
" a virtual private cloud environment such as Amazon EC2. CentreStack is "
"also available in the form of AMI image to facilitate creation of EC2 "
"instances. In this deployment scenario, the typical primary storage "
"connection is to the Amazon S3 storage. You can also setup CentreStack "
"solution in an environment like HP Helion (OpenStack) Cloud, with a "
"Windows Server 2025/2022/2019 connecting to OpenStack Swift storage."
msgstr "I dette udrulningsscenarie ville du implementere CentreStack-løsningen i et virtuelt privat cloud-miljø som Amazon EC2. CentreStack er også tilgængelig i form af et AMI-billede for at lette oprettelsen af EC2-instanser. I dette udrulningsscenarie er den typiske primære lagerforbindelse til Amazon S3-lageret. Du kan også opsætte CentreStack-løsningen i et miljø som HP Helion (OpenStack) Cloud, med en Windows Server 2025/2022/2019, der forbinder til OpenStack Swift-lager."

#: ../../index.rst:544
msgid "Multi-Site Deployment"
msgstr "Multi-Site Udrulning"

#: ../../index.rst:545
msgid "Please reference multi-site deployment."
msgstr "Henvis venligst til multi-site udrulning."

#: ../../index.rst:548
msgid "Security Consideration"
msgstr "Sikkerhedsovervejelser"

#: ../../index.rst:551
msgid "Access Clients and CentreStack"
msgstr "Adgangsklienter og CentreStack"

#: ../../index.rst:553
msgid ""
"The access client agents will be configured with an access end point in "
"the form of https://cloud.acme.com, where cloud.acme.com is the DNS name "
"of your CentreStack server. The communication from the access clients, "
"such as login request will be protected by SSL over HTTP (HTTPS)."
msgstr "Adgangsklientagenturerne vil blive konfigureret med et adgangspunkt i form af https://cloud.acme.com, hvor cloud.acme.com er DNS-navnet på din CentreStack-server. Kommunikationen fra adgangsklienterne, såsom loginanmodning, vil være beskyttet af SSL over HTTP (HTTPS)."

#: ../../index.rst:559
msgid ""
"We recommend using https://www.ssllabs.com/ to check out the strength of "
"your SSL certificate and whether or not it is compatible with iOS 9 and "
"above devices."
msgstr "Vi anbefaler at bruge https://www.ssllabs.com/ til at tjekke styrken af dit SSL-certifikat og om det er kompatibelt med iOS 9 og nyere enheder."

#: ../../index.rst:563
msgid "CentreStack and Active Directory"
msgstr "CentreStack og Active Directory"

#: ../../index.rst:565
msgid ""
"If the CentreStack is configured with Active Directory, CentreStack will "
"authenticate users on behalf of the active directory by contacting the "
"Active Directory over LDAP or LDAPS. There is no direct communication "
"between the access clients and the Active Directory."
msgstr "Hvis CentreStack er konfigureret med Active Directory, vil CentreStack autentificere brugere på vegne af Active Directory ved at kontakte Active Directory over LDAP eller LDAPS. Der er ingen direkte kommunikation mellem adgangsklienterne og Active Directory."

